import{_ as t,o as n,c as a,ag as r}from"./chunks/framework.KxDd3USm.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"11.7 课后考题","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"11-专业英语/90-课后考题.md","filePath":"11-专业英语/90-课后考题.md"}'),s={name:"11-专业英语/90-课后考题.md"};function o(i,e,d,c,g,l){return n(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="_11-7-课后考题" tabindex="-1">11.7 课后考题 <a class="header-anchor" href="#_11-7-课后考题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;11.7 课后考题&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>三篇短文各 5 空，共 15 题。先按正式考试方式连续做完，再看答案。</p></blockquote><h3 id="passage-1-requirements-engineering-第-1–5-题" tabindex="-1">Passage 1：Requirements Engineering（第 1–5 题） <a class="header-anchor" href="#passage-1-requirements-engineering-第-1–5-题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Passage 1：Requirements Engineering（第 1–5 题）&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Requirements engineering is the process of discovering, documenting, and maintaining what a software system should do. A well-written requirement should be clear, consistent, and <strong>(1)</strong>, so that testers can determine whether the implemented system satisfies it. During elicitation, analysts communicate with stakeholders to <strong>(2)</strong> their real needs rather than merely recording an initial solution. Because business conditions may change, approved requirements should be placed under configuration <strong>(3)</strong>. A traceability matrix links each requirement to design elements and test cases, making the impact of a proposed change easier to <strong>(4)</strong>. When a prototype is built, its main purpose is often to reduce uncertainty and obtain early <strong>(5)</strong> from users.</p><p><strong>1.</strong> A. testable　B. invisible　C. temporary　D. accidental<br><strong>2.</strong> A. delete　B. identify　C. encrypt　D. compile<br><strong>3.</strong> A. management　B. transmission　C. arithmetic　D. recursion<br><strong>4.</strong> A. postpone　B. assess　C. hide　D. randomize<br><strong>5.</strong> A. bandwidth　B. feedback　C. ciphertext　D. deadlock</p><h3 id="passage-2-transactions-and-data-protection-第-6–10-题" tabindex="-1">Passage 2：Transactions and Data Protection（第 6–10 题） <a class="header-anchor" href="#passage-2-transactions-and-data-protection-第-6–10-题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Passage 2：Transactions and Data Protection（第 6–10 题）&quot;">​</a></h3><p>A database transaction groups several operations into a single logical unit of work. Atomicity ensures that either all operations take effect or none <strong>(6)</strong>. Isolation prevents concurrently executing transactions from observing inappropriate <strong>(7)</strong> states. Durability means that committed changes survive system <strong>(8)</strong>. When sensitive records travel across an untrusted network, encryption transforms plaintext into <strong>(9)</strong> so that unauthorized parties cannot understand it. A cryptographic hash serves a different purpose: its digest can help detect unauthorized <strong>(10)</strong> of the data, but it does not by itself keep the data secret.</p><p><strong>6.</strong> A. do　B. are　C. have　D. make<br><strong>7.</strong> A. intermediate　B. permanent　C. public　D. graphical<br><strong>8.</strong> A. failures　B. queries　C. indexes　D. schemas<br><strong>9.</strong> A. metadata　B. ciphertext　C. bandwidth　D. source code<br><strong>10.</strong> A. compression　B. allocation　C. modification　D. scheduling</p><h3 id="passage-3-cloud-computing-and-machine-learning-第-11–15-题" tabindex="-1">Passage 3：Cloud Computing and Machine Learning（第 11–15 题） <a class="header-anchor" href="#passage-3-cloud-computing-and-machine-learning-第-11–15-题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Passage 3：Cloud Computing and Machine Learning（第 11–15 题）&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Cloud computing provides shared computing resources over a network on demand. Elasticity allows capacity to scale up or down as the workload <strong>(11)</strong>. In an Infrastructure as a Service model, the customer manages operating systems and applications, while the provider manages the physical infrastructure. In Software as a Service, complete applications are delivered to users over the <strong>(12)</strong>, and the provider manages most of the technology stack. Machine learning takes a different but increasingly related role: a model learns patterns from examples instead of being explicitly <strong>(13)</strong> for every possible case. To estimate how well it will handle unseen examples, data is commonly divided into training and test <strong>(14)</strong>. A model that memorizes noise in its training data but performs poorly on new data is said to be <strong>(15)</strong>.</p><p><strong>11.</strong> A. changes　B. decrypts　C. inherits　D. commits<br><strong>12.</strong> A. compiler　B. Internet　C. register　D. semaphore<br><strong>13.</strong> A. programmed　B. routed　C. normalized　D. signed<br><strong>14.</strong> A. locks　B. keys　C. sets　D. frames<br><strong>15.</strong> A. portable　B. overfitted　C. atomic　D. serialized</p><h3 id="综合阅读题-不属于下午固定案例-用于训练长文理解" tabindex="-1">综合阅读题（不属于下午固定案例，用于训练长文理解） <a class="header-anchor" href="#综合阅读题-不属于下午固定案例-用于训练长文理解" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;综合阅读题（不属于下午固定案例，用于训练长文理解）&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Read the incident report and answer the questions in Chinese.</p><blockquote><p>After a new version of an online ordering service was deployed, its response time increased sharply during peak hours. Monitoring data showed that CPU utilization remained moderate, but database latency rose as the number of requests increased. Engineers found that a frequently executed query scanned the entire Orders table because a useful index had been removed during migration. They restored the index and added the query to the regression test suite. Performance returned to normal. The team also updated its deployment checklist so that future schema changes would be reviewed before release.</p></blockquote><p><strong>16.</strong> <code>deployed</code> 在文中的含义是什么？<br><strong>17.</strong> 哪项监控证据说明 CPU 不是主要瓶颈？<br><strong>18.</strong> 响应变慢的直接技术原因是什么？<br><strong>19.</strong> <code>regression test suite</code> 的作用是什么？<br><strong>20.</strong> 更新部署检查清单属于“只修复当前问题”，还是还包含预防未来问题？请给出文本依据。</p><hr>',16)])])}const u=t(s,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,u as default};
